<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    fragment_switch_pair.xml
    =========================
    Diagram for a PAIRED crossover: two parallel main tracks with a
    diagonal crossover between them.  The pair always throws together,
    so one toggle governs both.

    Track geometry (train travels UPWARD):
    ───────────────────────────────────────
      ┃    ┃       ← both mains exit at top
      ┃   ╱┃
      ┃  ╱ ┃       ← crossover diagonal (left→right, between mains only)
      ┃ ╱  ┃
      ┃╱   ┃
      ┃    ┃       ← both mains enter at bottom

    Rail conventions (gauge = 20dp):
      • Left main:   full-height vertical pair               → GREEN
      • Right main:  full-height vertical pair               → GREEN
      • Crossover:   two parallel rails running diagonally
                     from the left main (bottom frog) up to
                     the right main (top frog), left → right.
                     Both crossover rails stay between the two
                     mains — they do not extend past either main.
                                                             → YELLOW (dim)

    Coordinate sketch:
      Left  main rails  x = [lL, lR]   full height
      Right main rails  x = [rL, rR]   full height   (lR < rL, gap between)
      Bottom frog  (lR, frogBottomY)
      Top    frog  (rL, frogTopY)
      Crossover inner rail:  (lR, frogBottomY) → (rL, frogTopY)
      Crossover outer rail:  20dp perpendicular offset toward the right
        outer start = (lR + 20·cos θ,  frogBottomY + 20·sin θ)
        outer end   = (rL + 20·cos θ,  frogTopY    + 20·sin θ)
        where θ is the perpendicular angle to the crossover direction.

    Colour convention (matches toggle):
      STRAIGHT  (checked / green)   → both mains green, crossover dim yellow.
      DIVERGING (unchecked / yellow) → crossover bright yellow, mains dim green.

    Implementation: SwitchPairView draws both mains and the crossover.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent">

    <com.controls.train.app.switches.view.SwitchPairView
        android:id="@+id/view_switch_pair"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:contentDescription="Switch pair diagram"
        app:switchThrown="false" />

</FrameLayout>